//! almondbread-ffi: the UniFFI surface of the Rust core for the Swift UI
//! (kb: decisions/rust-core, platform/rust-swift-ffi).
//!
//! Built as a static library into `AlmondbreadCoreFFI.xcframework`
//! (scripts/build-rust-xcframework.sh); the Swift bindings are generated by uniffi-bindgen
//! in library mode. Rule: nothing per pixel or per iteration crosses this boundary; bulk
//! data (orbits) moves as one copy into caller memory.
//!
//! - R1: version, coordinate parse/format, precision rule, reference selection, reference
//!   orbit with cancellation, and a no-op call for measuring the call overhead.
//! - R2b: the `Explorer` (explorer.rs, Apple targets): the renderer hosted in the app's
//!   `CAMetalLayer`, one `frame` call per display refresh; `palettes()`.
//! - Places: the catalogue of famous views (`places()`, `place()`, `random_place()`,
//!   `place_scale()`, `Explorer::go_to_place`; kb: synthesis/places). Thumbnails are app
//!   resources (`Sources/AlmondbreadKit/Resources/Places/<id>.heic`, `<id>@2x.heic`), never
//!   bytes over this boundary.

